message:
feat(silo/trace): record YCSB gate steps and installed stamps

Record each successful YCSB transaction's ordered R/W/M steps as a Q row
in gate_<thid>.log. Record the stamp about to be installed for every
Silo UPDATE as a V row in the same per-thread file. A Q row consumes the
pending trace txid; a missing txid is written as '-'. Retries discard both
pending txid and steps.

Use YCSB::id_ as an eight-byte stamp: ((thid + 1) << 48) | seq, with a
checked 16-bit writer and nonzero 48-bit per-thread sequence. Initial
load retains the key id as its genesis stamp. Only Silo's YCSB/v2 commit
path enables Q output and supplies the pending txid.

The TRACE=0 paths retain F's preprocessed line numbers through #line
restoration in ycsb.hh and the existing transaction.cc directives.
A search of all protocol YCSB paths found no post-load use of id_ as a
key or payload input; createKey() remains unused by the run path.

